================================================================================
Overrides table: a single `_overrides` layer replaces `_inferred` (add / modify / delete)
================================================================================

Context:
The Triple-Store Gateway exposed the R2RML mapping (`_data`) plus a write-only
`_inferred` / `__app` companion, so the app could add triples but never delete or
modify a mapped value (entity, relation, attribute), in either Delta mode. Spec:
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-24-overrides-table-design.md. One `*_overrides`
table now holds every change as `(subject, predicate, object, op, origin,
change_id, author, created_at)` with op = add | del and origin = user | reasoning
| cohort | community. The effective graph is (mapped U add rows) minus del rows.
A modification is an add of the new triple plus a del of the old one sharing one
change_id. The contract is the same on every backend; the mechanism is native.
Not run live: the SQL (Spark, Postgres) and Cypher are covered by unit tests on
the emitted statements, not by a warehouse / Lakebase / Neo4j round trip.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/graphdb/overrides.py (new)
   - Backend-neutral contract: op / origin vocabularies, validators,
     new_change_id, triple_key, unique_triples.
2. Delta: src/back/core/graphdb/delta/_table_naming.py, materialize.py,
   Builder.py, ReadStore.py, MaterializedStore.py, BuildPipeline.py
   - `_overrides` table, `_graph` view as an anti-join, new `_asserted` view
     (mapped + user adds - dels), one-time migration of legacy `_inferred` rows.
   - add / delete / modify on MaterializedStore with statement ordering that
     leaves the old value visible if interrupted (Delta has no multi-statement
     transaction). Build and purge only touch origin <> 'user'.
   - Builder.has_user_overrides(); ReadStore.synced_table_name returns `_asserted`.
3. Lakebase: src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py, FlatStore.py,
   OverrideOpsMixin.py (new), SimulationStore.py, InferredBreakdownMixin.py,
   _adjacency_ddl.py
   - `__overrides` companion (PK subject, predicate, object_hash, op), union view
     and `_asserted` view with anti-join, edits in one Postgres transaction via a
     COPY staging table, migration of legacy `__app` rows, reset_for_rebuild keeps
     the user rows. Sandboxes keep raw 3-column writes.
4. Neo4j: src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/OverrideJournal.py (new), Store.py
   - Edits are applied at once and journaled as :__Override nodes (journal first,
     then graph; two Bolt calls, not one transaction). Build keeps the journal and
     replay_overrides re-applies it. Simulation graphs are never journaled.
5. src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/MaterializedGraphBackend.py
   - supports_overrides, add_triples, modify_triple, reset_for_rebuild,
     replay_overrides (no-op default), insert_triples(origin=...).
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py,
   src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py
   - Full rebuild uses reset_for_rebuild (was drop + create, which destroyed user
     edits), then replay_overrides. Scheduled Lakebase builds load the bulk table.
7. src/back/core/graphdb/inferred_breakdown.py, src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py,
   src/back/core/graphdb/SearchCachePolicy.py, src/front/routes/dtwin.py,
   src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/BuildObjects.py
   - Inferred breakdown groups by origin (vocabulary heuristic for legacy rows);
     reads without derived triples use `_asserted`; edits mark the search cache
     pending so they show up at once.
8. src/back/core/graph_analysis/metrics/JobMetrics.py,
   cohort/CohortBuilder.py, community/CommunityMaterializer.py
   - Analytics snapshots `_asserted` only when a user override exists; cohort and
     community writers pass their origin and delete by origin (the previous
     DELETE FROM a view relation silently failed).
9. Tests: new tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_overrides.py,
   tests/units/graphdb/test_lakebase_overrides.py,
   tests/units/graphdb/test_neo4j_overrides.py; updated the existing
   Delta / Lakebase / build-pipeline / analytics / community tests.
10. Docs: docs/architecture.md, backend.md, user-guide.md, deployment.md,
    getting-started.md describe `_overrides`, `_graph`, `_asserted`.

Known limits:
   - Data Quality still snapshots the gateway VIEW (mapping only), by design.
   - Replace-style business-rule saves now leave user `del` rows for the removed
     triples (hidden, not erased).
   - SPARQL over the new views is a separate sub-project.

