Graph source labels: "Live graph" -> "Original Graph", "Live graph (inferred)" -> "Certified Graph"
================================================================================

Context:
The graph source options (Explorer, Query, Compare, Evaluate, Simulation help)
used "Live graph" for the asserted graph and "Live graph (inferred)" for the
graph with derived triples. Renamed for the user-facing vocabulary: the
asserted graph is the "Original Graph", the inferred one is the "Certified
Graph". Text only: option values (live, live:inferred), CSS classes, element
ids and identifiers (LIVE_INFERRED, _is_live_graph, test names) are unchanged.

Changes:
1. Templates, static JS, docs and tests (54 files under src/front, src/api,
   src/back, docs, README.md, tests): "Live graph (inferred)" -> "Certified
   Graph"; every other "live graph" -> "Original Graph" (articles adjusted,
   "a live graph" -> "an Original Graph"). Includes the Compare and Evaluate
   labels, the Scenario how-to, the help modal and the Knowledge Graph source
   dropdown.
2. Not changed, on purpose: src/agents/** (agent prompts and tool docstrings
   read by the LLM) and src/mcp-server/** (MCP tool outputs). Both fall under
   the AI feature lifecycle gate (.cursor/12-ai-feature-lifecycle.mdc): a prompt
   or tool-description change needs an eval delta first. They still say "live
   graph" and need a follow-up with an eval run.
3. Exception, committed with the rest: src/back/core/mcp_tools.py is the MCP
   tool catalogue, and the description of the select_simulation tool (read by
   LLM clients) now says "Original Graph". This is a tool-description wording
   change that has NOT been through an eval delta; it should be evaluated (or
   reverted) under the AI feature lifecycle gate.

